// ==WindhawkModReadme==
/*
# Taskbar AI Usage

See how much of your AI subscription you have left in one place. Get a glimpse
of all your accounts on the taskbar: Dynamic rings fill as you use your quota.
A Fluent flyout shows the details of every limit, time for the next reset and
whether you are burning through it faster than the clock.

![Claude flyout above the taskbar tiles](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sof2245/taskbar-ai-usage/main/docs/images/hero.png)

### Supported services

* **Claude.** 5-hour session, weekly, Fable weekly, model and surface limits,
  and monthly extra usage.
* **ChatGPT / Codex.** 5-hour session, weekly, additional rate limits such as
  Codex Spark, and prepaid credits.
* **Antigravity.** Gemini and other-model pools, each with session and weekly
  quotas.
* **GitHub Copilot.** Monthly AI credits.

### Features

* **Multiple tiles and accounts.** Pick up to three quotas to show on the tiles.
  The color moves from green to yellow, orange and red as you pass your
  thresholds.
* **Pace at a glance.** A dot on each ring marks where you would be if you
  spread your usage evenly over the window. An indicator estimates when you will
  hit your next limit.
* **Fluent flyout.** Compact rows per quota with its reset countdown, banked
  free resets, and direct access to the provider dashboard. Click to show or get
  a glance on hover.
* **Sign in your way.** Accounts get automatically detected and added or opt to
  sign-in each account on its own. It borrows the Claude Code, Codex, Visual
  Studio or GitHub CLI login you are already using. Antigravity can read its
  running local session.
* **Notifications.** Optional notifications tell you when usage crosses the
  threshold you choose, with the next reset time.
* **Lenguajes/语言.** Localizada completamente al Chino (Simplificado) y Español
  (internacional). 完全本地化为简体中文和西班牙语（国际通用）。

| Codex | Antigravity | Copilot |
|---|---|---|
| ![Codex flyout](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sof2245/taskbar-ai-usage/main/docs/images/flyout-codex.png) | ![Antigravity flyout](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sof2245/taskbar-ai-usage/main/docs/images/flyout-antigravity.png) | ![Copilot flyout](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sof2245/taskbar-ai-usage/main/docs/images/flyout-copilot.png) |

![Settings window, Display page](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sof2245/taskbar-ai-usage/main/docs/images/settings-display.png)

### Getting started

1. Enable the mod. If Claude Code, Codex, Visual Studio or GitHub CLI is already
   signed in on this PC, its account shows up on its own.
2. For anything else, click the **+** tile (or right-click a tile and choose
   **Settings**), add the account and click **Sign in**.
3. Left-click a tile for its flyout. Right-click it to refresh, open the
   dashboard, hide accounts or open settings.

If you use **Taskbar AI Quota Bars**, disable it first. Both mods would poll the
same accounts, and they don't share accounts or sign-ins.

### Privacy and disclaimers

* Credentials never leave your PC. The mod talks only to each provider's sign-in
  and usage endpoints and sends no telemetry.
* A borrowed sign-in is read on every poll and never written, refreshed or
  stored. It never sends a prompt.
* Usage comes from undocumented endpoints that can change and stop working
  without notice. The author is not responsible for its accuracy.
* Neither this mod nor its author is affiliated with Anthropic, OpenAI, Google,
  GitHub, Microsoft or any other usage provider.

### Credits

* Based on a fork of
  [Taskbar AI Quota Bars](https://github.com/Cleroth/windhawk-taskbar-ai-quota)
  by Cleroth.
* The flyout and button styling come from
  [Taskbar Fluent Media Player](https://github.com/Salyts/Taskbar-Fluent-Media-Player)
  by Salyts.
* Provider logos come from [Simple Icons](https://simpleicons.org)
  (CC0); the Copilot logo is from
  [Primer Octicons](https://github.com/primer/octicons) (MIT, GitHub Inc.).
* Claude, Anthropic, OpenAI, Codex, Gemini, Antigravity, GitHub and Copilot are
  trademarks of their owners. Their names and logos appear only to identify
  which account a tile belongs to.

### Report a bug

Found a problem or have an idea?
[Open an issue on GitHub](https://github.com/Sof2245/taskbar-ai-usage/issues).
*/
